    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71125.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "The first time I met her was actually on the campaign trail because she was very involved in helping us flip those seven congressional seats in California. So I met her a little while before, and yes, it was absolutely surreal. But I was, you know, she's this little woman who I think she's either 79 or she's turned 80. I think she's turned 80. And it's just like, how are you like this? But when I had the honor of going on a couple of these things that are called co-dels, they're congressional delegations, and they're trips, basically, for different reasons. And so I went on two with her. One was to the Munich Security Conference, because I was on armed services. And the second was to the Northern Triangle and to the border. the US Mexican border because of everything that was happening at that point with ICE. and the immigration crisis. So just on those trips, she was, you know, I was at 32 at that point, maybe even 31. And she has so much energy. Just everyone, she's famous for this. Like she just runs you into the ground. The woman does not sleep. She just like is just go, go, go constantly. And I don't know how she's done it for this many years. at her age and in those high heels. I just don't know. She's got something, some kind of crazy trick, I guess.",
