    "turn_text": "at the election. And then, um, and then I was kind of very quickly trying to figure a way out, but it was, you know, it's hard. You're in, you're in this kind of position. You're in an elected position. You, um, the, marriage story is kind of part of your campaign, right? Like, it's just, it just is for every politician. Um, and you are also, uh, you know, he always, I always had that threat. I always had that threat that, and I knew pretty much what he was going to use, right? It's rocket science to figure it out. I didn't know what pictures he had and there were ones that, you know, I didn't even know he'd taken. But, um, but I, it was, it was just a matter of time. And because every time that I would go, that I would have to go back to the district and stay at my house. I was just dreading it. When I'd go back, we would get into a fight every time that would involve him, basically not letting me sleep. It was",
