    "turn_idx": 211,
    "turn_text": "you know, I've said this to other people before too, but that I think if maybe if I were a more experienced politician, if I were somebody who had been in office before, who had seen other people kind of weather the storm of scandal, it might have been different. But you know, my staff was also, they were all new to this and they were going through the same things. miserable for them. It was, you know, I think the whole thing was horrifying for them. And I hated what it was putting the woman through. I don't even like to use her name ever because I don't want any more attention to go to her. But I, you know, I think that there's just, there are these other aspects of like, the personal side of it of just who I felt like I was impacting and how survivable it was, not just in terms of electability and of surviving an election, but actually just making it through as a person.",
