    "turn_idx": 213,
    "turn_text": "I think that's part of why when I stepped down, I gave that defiant speech and I wanted to show back up and say, okay, you might have won that round, but you're not gonna win the whole thing. But yeah, I mean, I hate that they won. I hate to feel that they won. And I guess I hope that more than anything, my resignation is like a lesson and a turning point for us to say that the women who have these kinds of things happen to them are the victims and not the other way around. And, you know, to really, I think it's forced us to have a reckoning around a lot of these difficult subjects. And I hope that that continues. And I'm hopeful for what it implies for future, for, you know, future incidents like this, because it's not going away. I mean, people are sending these photos left and right. And, you know, the abusive, abusive acts is always going to be a factor in life. And it shouldn't stop. women from, you know, seeking these kinds of positions and from being able to change the world.",
