    "turn_idx": 336,
    "turn_text": "she's just incredible. And I think that, you know, we got in before any of the other major organizations did. And I think we really did give her that boost. And she won, she made it to a runoff in the primary, then she won the primary by a huge margin. She won the run off by a huge margin. And so now I think she's got one of the best chances at flipping a red seat blue in the fall. And I know that we'll always be able to say, while we were one of the first ones in. And so I'm excited about that. And there are a few others. But I am proud to say that our organization is a risk-taking one. I make no pretenses that all of our candidates are going to win. I'm not here. to get on the ones that we know for sure are winners. We want to give people an opportunity and we want to take the Longshot candidates. We want to be the ones that are really supporting people who we want to have in public office and who we want to have as the next generation of leaders, the next generation of women who are making it and who are representing all of us, but that need an extra boost to do so. And that means maybe they'll win now, maybe they won't win now, but they'll be there later. And then the last thing that we're doing with her time is really pushing for these issues, these issues that I outline in the book and the legislative solutions that we know exist. I was so glad that they paid so much attention to the Violence Against Women Act that Biden introduced and did for him for doing that in the 90s, but we have to take it to the next level. And I talk about that in my book as one of the priority pieces of legislation, the fact that it's stalled at the Senate is a fucking embarrassment. So, you know, I think there's a lot of potential there. And then after, you know, after all of this happens, after, you know, after the election, after the inauguration, We have to immediately start thinking about 2022, because if we flip the Senate and the White House, the House's major jeopardy in 2022 with redistricting and everything like that. So I want to be involved in that. And I know that it's a change to be the more behind the scenes role. But I feel like I can have an interesting hybrid of behind the scenes and in front of the scenes, but not as an elected official.",
